{
  "feature": "Quiet integer UnaryPlus operands and FULL conditions in static USER ternary-left coalesce selectors",
  "status": "Independently reviewed bounded increment; family and full core remain partial.",
  "target": "PHP 8.5.10 CLI NTS64; project-local pinned oracle and recorded profile.",
  "behavior": "The quiet selector certificate admits UnaryPlus over source-authenticated closed values when existing pure coercion yields a warning-free signed64 integer. It returns exact PINT for NULL/BOOL/INT/full numeric INT STRING, including old byte-positive PLUS leaves. Only the dedicated FULL fallback requires old-byte=None; all old Some byte proofs remain literal. INT0 stays nonnull in COALESCE and differs in truth from STRING00.",
  "implementation": {
    "source": "e0f0a5e210dfe40d34ce94f825d833fe176495de",
